# =============================================================================
# .gitignore -- Reproducing World Models (Ha & Schmidhuber, 2018)
#
# Measured sizes on this machine (RTX 3060 Laptop):
#   data/raw/           ~55 GB   raw CarRacing frames, 26 MB per rollout
#   data/*_frames.npy   ~2.8 GB  memmap frame cache (per 100 rollouts)
#   data/*_latents/     ~150 MB  encoded latents, float16
#   runs/               ~640 MB  checkpoints (two thirds is Adam state)
# All of it is regenerable by re-running the pipeline; see README.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Data: raw rollouts and everything derived from them --------------------
# Exclude directory *contents*, not the directory itself: git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded, and the tiny provenance files
# below must survive.
data/raw/*
data/pilot/*
data/explore/*

# memmap frame caches
data/*.npy

# latent datasets: exclude the arrays, keep the index (mean/std + provenance)
data/*_latents/*.npy

# small provenance files that document exactly what was collected
!data/**/manifest.json
!data/**/index.json

# ---- Training artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# Each checkpoint is ~42 MB (14 MB weights + 28 MB Adam moments). The optimiser
# state only matters for resuming, which finished runs no longer do.
runs/**
!runs/**/
# keep the training curves: cited as evidence in notes/Note3.md
!runs/**/log.jsonl

# ---- Generated figures ------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerate with scripts/vae/recon_grid.py and scripts/mdn/dream_rollout.py.
# Force-add a specific figure when a note cites it: git add -f artifacts/x.png
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- Virtual environments ---------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Logs, temp files, secrets ----------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
.env
.env.*
